messages:
maria: quick heads-up — I pushed a tiny TF change that adds a per-model ConfigMap sync so runtime flags live with infra instead of being baked into images. can someone quick-check for secret leakage and rollout semantics? diff excerpt below.

```hcl
resource \"kubernetes_config_map\" \"model_flags\" {
  for_each = toset(var.models)
  metadata {
    name      = \"model-flags-${each.key}\"
    namespace = var.namespace
    labels = { app = \"inference\" }
  }
  data = {
    \"flags.json\" = file("${path.module}/flags/${each.key}.json")
  }
}

# deployment template annotation to force restart on configmap change
metadata {
  annotations = {
    \"checksum/configmap-model-flags\" = sha256(file("${path.module}/flags/${var.current_model}.json"))
  }
}
```

maria: also added a terraform loop so new models don't need hand edits. pipeline will `kubectl apply` the CM during deploy.

sam: quick looks: overall ok. two notes — file() reads repo files at plan time, make sure CI copies the flags/* files into the module dir for remote runs or use a data source (s3) if kept out of repo.

sam: also: don't put secrets in flags.json. if a flag needs a secret, store a k8s Secret and reference via secretKeyRef in the pod env.

jordan: agree with sam. for the rolling update we use the checksum annotation pattern already, here's the snippet we use in other services: 

```yaml
template:
  metadata:
    annotations:
      checksum/configmap-model-flags: {{ checksum file("flags/{{ .Values.model }}.json") }}
```

jordan: TF-side: prefer `for_each = { for m in var.models: m => m }` so keys are predictable. otherwise the name interpolation can change when list order shifts.

li: small perf/ops thing — when we have 50+ models the configmap size becomes large. consider splitting large per-model blobs into per-model single-key CMs (which you're doing) and using `maxUnavailable` tuning on the deployment to avoid thundering restarts.

infra-bot: tfplan: ran on branch/maria/configmap-model-flags — PLAN: 1 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy. tfsec: WARNING: possible plaintext secret detected in flags/beta.json line 3. (rule: generic-secrets)

maria: thanks infra-bot — pulling that file and swapping to secret ref now. will push a fix in a minute.

sam: also can you add a quick test in deploy pipeline: `kubectl create configmap --dry-run=client --from-file=flags/<model>.json -o yaml` to validate format before apply.

maria: doing that. i'll squash and merge in ~30m unless any objections. @sam can you watch the canary after merge?

sam: yep i'll monitor logs/latency and the canary dashboard. :thumbsup:

maria: thanks all — keeping the PR small, will post final sha once merged.
